Try on Me App

The Base: Your stored "Master Face" photo.
The Overlay: A high-quality digital "color swatch" or a "virtual collar" that is rendered specifically over your neck area using the coordinates found by MediaPipe.
The Result: It looks like you are wearing a shirt of that exact color. Even though it's a static photo, the WebXR tech ensures the digital collar "sits" correctly on your shoulders.

Spreadsheet link:
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1AwfSdW0sUzK045wrVirPuK_oCsP-PTr67b8q4sG0aQE/edit?gid=0#gid=0

steps keep google link:
https://keep.google.com/?source=gemini#home

By using IndexedDB, you get the best of both worlds: the "memory" of a database without the privacy risks or hosting costs of a cloud server. 
Your face photo stays on your Android phone, but it’s still there every time you walk into a store.
